-- Two mutually recursive declarations that carry the SAME `where` clause
-- (`docs/design/static-dispatch-spike.md` §6.4, §7.2, §8.1, §8.2).
--
-- `core/Dict.beni`'s `removeHelp` and `removeHelpEQGT` are this shape, and
-- they are the pair the C1 rewrite of §5.3 cannot avoid: each one's
-- annotation promises `k.compare`, each one calls the other, and neither
-- can be checked before the other. So the evidence parameter of §8.1 has to
-- be on BOTH before either body is lowered, and the call each makes to the
-- other has to pass its own `$m$0` straight through.
--
-- What a mistake here looks like: `$m$0` passed as a beni argument rather
-- than in front of it, so `largest` receives the comparator where it
-- expects the list; or an evidence parameter on one of the two and not the
-- other, so the call is one argument short and JavaScript runs it anyway,
-- binding `undefined` and comparing against it. Neither is visible in
-- `--stage=types`; both print the wrong answer here.
--
-- **A PIN, not a regression test.** This shape already worked on `cb63a46`,
-- before S6a: it was added because nothing in the corpus covered it, not
-- because anything broke. `appendSite`'s forwarding of a shared group's
-- constraint (§6.4) and the evidence parameter on both headers are what it
-- holds still, and they are the two things a change to §7.2's numbering
-- would move first.
import Node exposing (Program)
import String


-- `largest xs best` is the biggest of `best` and everything in `xs`.
largest : List a, a -> a
    where a.compare : a, a -> Order
largest xs best =
    case xs of
        [] ->
            best

        x :: rest ->
            step rest x best


-- One step of `largest`, split out so the recursion is mutual rather than
-- direct — and written with the dot-call rather than `>`, so the pair
-- exercises both surfaces of §1.3 through one evidence parameter.
step : List a, a, a -> a
    where a.compare : a, a -> Order
step xs x best =
    case x.compare best of
        GT ->
            largest xs x

        _ ->
            largest xs best


main : Program
main =
    Node.printLines
        [ String.fromInt (largest [ 3, 9, 4 ] 0)
        , String.fromInt (largest [] 7)
        , largest [ "pear", "apple", "fig" ] ""
        , largest [ "a" ] "b"
        ]
